moira (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package 1: Claude quota collection through the chained status-line
    command with a minimal privacy-safe cache, fail-closed validation and
    stale-data handling.
  * Package 2: Codex quota collection through the documented app-server
    read-only rate-limit method, weekly exhaustion semantics, unavailable
    and parse-error states, compact mode.
  * Package 3: local History tab with schema v4 SQLite storage, selectable
    24h/7d/30d/90d ranges and per-service filters, quota series with reset
    transitions, exact daily token statistics from official Codex account
    usage (Claude remains percentage-only), and history deletion.
  * Package 4: per-provider collection toggles, typed alert rules, native
    desktop and NTFY notification channels with deduplicated exhaustion,
    recovery, reset and error events, and sanitized diagnostics with copy
    actions.
  * Package 5: deterministic CSV/JSON export, persisted configuration v3,
    update checks with strict SemVer parsing, French localization with
    English fallback, and correction passes closing persisted-version and
    artifact-hygiene gaps.
  * Package 6: privacy-minimal agent activity visibility — a spinner and
    terminal state for Claude Code, Hermes and Moira-owned Codex app-server
    sessions, recorded through owned hooks and the documented Codex
    app-server protocol with hashed identities and an independent turn
    lifecycle; plus Debian policy compliance and reproducible packaging.

